[%# One level of the SNMP tree. A branch is a <details> so the browser supplies
    disclosure and keyboard toggling; its <summary> is the marker alone.

    The label is a sibling of the <details>, not a child of it: a closed
    <details> hides everything in it that is not the summary, and the label has
    to be readable whether the branch is open or shut. It comes first so that
    the child list, which follows inside the <details>, lands beneath it; the
    stylesheet lifts the marker out of flow into the row's left gutter.

    Children arrive on first open, unless the server already rendered them
    because a node opens itself or a search opened the tree down to a hit. A
    branch that arrives filled carries no fetch at all: `toggle` fires on close
    as well as open, and it fires in Chromium for a branch that arrives already
    open, either of which would swap one flat level over the subtree. %]
[%- FOREACH node IN nodes -%]
<li class="nd_snmp-row">
  [%- INCLUDE 'ajax/device/snmplabel.tt' node=node -%]
  [%- IF node.has_children -%]
  [%# both the fetch and the accessible name go on the details: the toggle
      event fires there, and the browser exposes the details, not the empty
      summary, as the named group %]
  <details class="nd_snmp-branch" aria-label="Expand [% node.label | html_entity %]"[% ' open' IF node.open %]
           [%- UNLESS node.children.size %]
           hx-get="[% uri_base | none %]/ajax/content/device/[% device | uri %]/snmptree/[% node.oid | uri %]"
           hx-target="find ul" hx-swap="innerHTML" hx-trigger="toggle once"
           [%- END %]>
    <summary></summary>
    <ul class="nd_snmp-children">
      [%- IF node.children.size -%]
      [%- INCLUDE 'ajax/device/snmptree.tt' nodes=node.children -%]
      [%- END -%]
    </ul>
  </details>
  [%- END -%]
</li>
[%- END -%]
